Microsoft Learn: Monitor Your Azure Virtual Machines with Azure Monitor

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Monitor Your Azure Virtual Machines with Azure Monitor
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to monitor Azure Virtual Machines using Azure Monitor, collect host and guest operating system data, analyze performance metrics, and troubleshoot VM health issues using Metrics Explorer and VM Insights.

This module focused on Azure Monitor capabilities for Virtual Machines, including collecting host metrics, guest operating system performance data, event logs, and using monitoring tools to proactively manage Azure infrastructure.

Step 1: Understanding Azure Monitor

The module introduced Azure Monitor as Microsoft's centralized monitoring platform for Azure resources.

Azure Monitor collects and analyzes:

Metrics
Logs
Performance counters
Event logs
Alerts
Telemetry data
Primary goals:
Monitor health
Identify performance issues
Troubleshoot problems
Improve reliability
Optimize resource usage
Example:
Azure VM
      ↓
Azure Monitor
      ↓
Metrics + Logs
      ↓
Dashboards & Alerts

The module emphasized that Azure Monitor is the primary monitoring solution for Azure resources.

Step 2: Understanding Monitoring for Azure Virtual Machines

The training covered why VM monitoring is important.

Common issues administrators need to detect:
High CPU usage
Memory pressure
Disk bottlenecks
Network latency
Application failures
Operating system issues
Benefits of monitoring:
Proactive issue detection
Performance optimization
Capacity planning
Faster troubleshooting
Key lesson learned:

Monitoring should be enabled before problems occur, not after.

Step 3: Understanding VM Host Data

A major focus of the module was host monitoring.

Host data comes from the Azure platform itself rather than the operating system running inside the VM.

Host metrics include:
CPU utilization
Network traffic
Disk throughput
Disk operations
Availability status
Example:
Azure Hypervisor
        ↓
Host Metrics
        ↓
Azure Monitor
Benefits:
No agent required
Automatically available
Platform-level visibility

Host metrics are one of the most important AZ-104 monitoring concepts.

Step 4: Understanding Azure Metrics

The training introduced Azure Metrics.

Metrics are numerical measurements collected over time.

Common VM metrics:
Metric	Purpose
Percentage CPU	Processor utilization
Disk Read Operations	Storage performance
Disk Write Operations	Storage activity
Network In	Incoming traffic
Network Out	Outgoing traffic
Available Memory	Resource utilization
Example:
CPU Usage
9 AM → 20%
12 PM → 85%
3 PM → 40%
Benefits:
Performance monitoring
Trend analysis
Capacity planning

Metrics form the foundation of Azure monitoring.

