VM Insights is commonly tested on AZ-104.

Step 7: Host Metrics vs Guest Metrics

The training compared platform monitoring and guest monitoring.

Host Metrics

Collected by Azure automatically.

Examples:

CPU percentage
Network throughput
Disk operations
Guest Metrics

Collected from inside the operating system.

Examples:

Memory usage
Running processes
Service status
Event logs
Comparison:
Type	Source
Host Metrics	Azure Platform
Guest Metrics	Operating System
Key lesson learned:

Guest monitoring requires an agent.

Step 8: Collecting Performance Counters

The module introduced performance counters.

Performance counters measure operating system performance.

Common counters:
Counter	Purpose
Processor Time	CPU usage
Available Memory	Memory health
Disk Queue Length	Storage performance
Network Throughput	Network activity
Example:
Memory Available
8 GB → Healthy
500 MB → Problem
Benefits:
Resource monitoring
Bottleneck detection
Capacity planning

Performance counters are collected through Azure Monitor Agent and VM Insights.

Step 9: Understanding Azure Monitor Agent (AMA)

The training introduced Azure Monitor Agent.

The Azure Monitor Agent collects guest operating system data and sends it to Azure Monitor.

Data collected:
Performance counters
Event logs
Monitoring telemetry
Benefits:
Centralized monitoring
Simplified data collection
Improved visibility
Key concept learned:

For guest operating system monitoring, the Azure Monitor Agent must be installed.

